      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The protective effect of GIK infusion on the ischaemic myocardium was assessed by isovolumic function tests and electron microscopy. There were two control groups, group 1 hearts underwent 2 hours of continous normothermic cross-perfusion and group 2 hearts endured 2 hours of ischaemia. Group 3 hearts were administered GIK solution prior to ischaemic arrest. The group 3 hearts showed less loss of contractile force and contractile velocity from the ischaemic period compared to group 2 hearts, but no benfit was shown in terms of compliance. Electron microscopic examination showed slightly less damage in the group 3 hearts compared to group 2 hearts. Group 1 hearts maintained better function than either of the other two groups. Ultrastructure was not examined in group 1 hearts. A slight protective effect of GIK on the ischaemic myocardium was thus confirmed."},
